    </div>

    <div class="section-title" style="margin-top: 2px;">Tasks Completed (7 pts)</div>
    <div class="instruction-sub">(Describe the main tasks that have been assigned and already completed. Max 250 words).</div>
    <table class="report-table" style="margin-bottom: 5px; font-size: 7.6pt;">
      <tr>
        <th style="width: 70%; padding: 2px 4px;">Task Completed</th>
        <th style="width: 30%; padding: 2px 4px;">Team Member</th>
      </tr>
      <tr><td style="padding: 2px 4px;">Implemented C++ Singly Linked List transaction audit ledger and pointer cleanup</td><td style="padding: 2px 4px;">Pari Singhal</td></tr>
      <tr><td style="padding: 2px 4px;">Built FIFO Audit Review Queue in C++ for sequential expense claim processing</td><td style="padding: 2px 4px;">Pari Singhal</td></tr>
      <tr><td style="padding: 2px 4px;">Programmed Jaccard Token Text Similarity algorithm to catch copycat campaigns</td><td style="padding: 2px 4px;">Pari Singhal</td></tr>
      <tr><td style="padding: 2px 4px;">Designed Admin Verification Dashboard UI and approval action controls</td><td style="padding: 2px 4px;">Pari Singhal</td></tr>
      <tr><td style="padding: 2px 4px;">Wired Subprocess IPC pipe bridge between Python server and C++ engine</td><td style="padding: 2px 4px;">Pari Singhal</td></tr>
      <tr><td style="padding: 2px 4px;">Built single-page web layout, navigation bar, and 4-tier role dashboards</td><td style="padding: 2px 4px;">Yashasvi Sharma</td></tr>
      <tr><td style="padding: 2px 4px;">Created simulated checkout modal and automatic 80G tax receipt generator</td><td style="padding: 2px 4px;">Yashasvi Sharma</td></tr>
      <tr><td style="padding: 2px 4px;">Connected frontend JavaScript fetch calls to backend REST API endpoints</td><td style="padding: 2px 4px;">Yashasvi Sharma</td></tr>
      <tr><td style="padding: 2px 4px;">Designed 3NF Relational Database schema and SQLite persistence layer</td><td style="padding: 2px 4px;">Divyanka Kumari</td></tr>
      <tr><td style="padding: 2px 4px;">Built Expense Receipt and Invoice Image Upload modal with image lightbox</td><td style="padding: 2px 4px;">Divyanka Kumari</td></tr>
      <tr><td style="padding: 2px 4px;">Helped with CSS color styling and basic documentation formatting</td><td style="padding: 2px 4px;">Shreya Kumari</td></tr>
      <tr><td style="padding: 2px 4px;">Cross-device mobile testing, automated test runs, and final user guide</td><td style="padding: 2px 4px;">All Members</td></tr>
    </table>

    <div class="section-title">Challenges/Roadblocks (7 pts)</div>
    <div class="instruction-sub">(Describe the challenges that you have faced or are facing so far and how you plan to solve them. Max 300 words).</div>
    <div class="content-box" style="font-size: 7.7pt; line-height: 1.2; padding: 4px 6px; margin-bottom: 5px;">
      <p>Connecting our compiled C++ engine to the web server gave us plenty of late-night headaches in the lab this phase. Subprocess IPC was easily our toughest technical hurdle. When Python launched <code>engine.exe</code> on Windows, the C++ output kept getting trapped in the stdout pipe buffer. Our web requests would just hang forever waiting for a response. After spending two evenings debugging, Pari realized Windows handles stream flushing differently than Linux. We fixed it by adding explicit <code>fflush(stdout)</code> calls inside C++ and reading pipe buffers cleanly in Python.</p>
      <p>Another big pain point was keeping campaign balances accurate across user dashboards. During early tests, whenever a fundraiser uploaded an invoice, our JavaScript immediately subtracted the money from the public balance. That completely defeated our audit rule! We sat down and restructured both the SQL queries and frontend state so only expenses with an approved status actually deduct from available funds. Mobile responsiveness was another annoying headache. When we opened the receipt image modal on our phones, Android browsers allowed the background page to keep scrolling, which broke the lightbox position. Divyanka and Pari fixed this with body scroll locks and responsive CSS media queries. Finally, managing GitHub commits with all four of us pushing code simultaneously caused frustrating merge conflicts in week one. Yashasvi set up strict branch rules: everyone had to work on their own feature branch, test locally with our test suite, and get a pull request reviewed before merging into main. That saved us from overwriting each other's work.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="section-title">Project Outcome/Deliverables (2 pts)</div>
    <div class="instruction-sub">(Describe what are the key outcomes / deliverables of the project. Max 200 words).</div>
    <div class="content-box" style="font-size: 7.7pt; line-height: 1.2; padding: 4px 6px; margin-bottom: 5px;">
      <p>We are delivering a complete, fully working web application where every single rupee can be tracked from donor to beneficiary: (1) Our compiled C++ engine (<code>engine.exe</code>) featuring a custom linked list ledger, FIFO review queue, Jaccard similarity detector, and heuristic risk analyzer. (2) A lightweight Python REST server with zero third-party packages that communicates with the C++ binary via IPC pipes. (3) A 3NF SQLite database storing users, campaigns, donation entries, and uploaded receipt proofs. (4) An interactive web frontend with custom dashboards for Guests, Donors, Fundraisers, and Admins, featuring a donation checkout modal, receipt lightbox, and instant 80G tax receipt generator. (5) Automated test scripts covering role permissions, financial balances, and end-to-end API calls. (6) Our full GitHub repository with commit history, documentation, and a viva prep guide.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="section-title">Progress Overview (2 pts)</div>
    <div class="instruction-sub">(Summarize how much of the project is done, what’s behind schedule, what’s ahead of schedule. Max 200 words.)</div>
    <div class="content-box" style="font-size: 7.7pt; line-height: 1.2; padding: 4px 6px; margin-bottom: 2px;">
      <p>Our team hit 100% completion on all our Phase 3 goals and we are completely on schedule for our final evaluation. In Phase 2, we only had command-line outputs and C++ modules running in the terminal. Now, the entire platform is live in the browser. Pari finished the C++ algorithms and IPC bridge, Yashasvi built the frontend dashboards and 80G receipt generator, Divyanka completed the database and receipt upload modals, and Shreya assisted with UI styles and test documentation. We ran all our automated test scripts and everything passed with zero errors. We also spent time testing the app on our phones and laptops using Chrome and Edge to confirm there are no broken layouts or buttons. There is nothing pending or behind schedule, and we are ready for the final demo.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="footer-row">
    <span>Page 4</span>
  </div>
</div>

